TRIC, measured not argued:** `git diff --name-only <branch> main -- scripts` lists paths differing in **PRESENCE** as well as content (proven directly: `tmp-s1664-lock.mjs` is on main, absent from `lane/b`, and *that asymmetry alone* is why it drifts), so deleting the files makes them drift **from the other side** — a 125-file sweep takes `lane/b` from **5 → 126** and lanes a/c/d to **139 / 186 / 146**, until all four lanes are refreshed. The cure is 25× the disease. **(2) 26 OF THE 151 ARE CITED RETAINED EVIDENCE, NOT DEBRIS** (measured by grepping each basename across the tracked corpus, excluding self-references): `tmp-s1046-unshipped.mjs` alone is cited **24×**, is named in a ratified master's NO list as *"a historical artefact retired by comment under the RETENTION LAW; read it, cite it, **never edit or delete it**"*, and is the subject of a live pre-flight `grep -Fc` that a sweep would turn into a false STOP; `gate-battery.mjs:16` and `gate-battery.test.mjs:9` cite `tmp-s1146-gate.mjs:51` **by line**; `tmp-s1140-probe2/probe3.mjs` are the paired-control instruments behind task-037's diagnosis. **(3)** the RETENTION LAW and `CLAUDE.md` §4.10 both say supersede/move, never erase. ➡️ **CURED AT THE GENERATOR THIS FIRE, WHICH COSTS NOTHING AND CANNOT BACKFIRE:** `scripts/fire.md` §4 now tells fires to write one-shot splice helpers to **`/tmp/s<N>-*.mjs`** — outside the repo, where they can never enter the run surface. s1665 wrote every one of its own there; s1045's own handoff already called its untracked lock scratch *"harmless"*, so this is an existing precedent made explicit rather than a new policy. ⓘ **A probe that PRODUCED EVIDENCE is the opposite case and still belongs in `scripts/`, committed and cited** — that is the line the corpus already draws, and those 26 files are exactly it. 🚫 **NO GUARD IS PROPOSED AND NONE SHOULD BE BUILT:** "one-shot helper vs retained probe" is a judgement, so a red guard would fire on every legitimate probe and be excused into