✅ **F-1660-1 (s1660 2026-08-11, MEASURED ON A BOARD THAT REPORTED ITSELF DRY FOR THE FOURTH CONSECUTIVE FIRE — AN OWNER RULING, MERGED AND GATED TWO DAYS AGO, HAS BEEN SILENTLY REVERSED ON MAIN FOR ~15 HOURS, AND THE GUARD THAT WATCHES THAT SURFACE STAYED GREEN THROUGHOUT BECAUSE AGREEMENT IS EXACTLY WHAT IT ASSERTS.)** 🧭 **HOW I FOUND IT:** the board was dry and s1659's NEXT(B) pointed at the `planned` leaves, so I priced them per §2E — and checked the owner's own 2026-08-09 rulings roundup rather than the leaf titles, per Mistake #4. Item 2 of that roundup reads *"F-E2S-3 RULED: de-list now, socket later … FIRE-AUTHORABLE, two masters, the de-list first"*, and the row two lines below it (F-1608-2, an OWNER'S DESK item) states as settled fact *"Both maps are currently door-de-listed per F-E2S-3, so nothing is blocked meanwhile."* ✗ **BOTH ARE FALSE ON MAIN TODAY, AND I PROVED IT WITH THE PRODUCT RATHER THAN A LEDGER:** `node scripts/gr-sim.mjs --contract=e2-hill-mine --seed=e2-hill-mine-01 --policy=idle` **runs a full contract and emits a view — no mode supplied, no throw.** `public/skill.md`'s public door fence lists `e2-hill-mine`, `e2-incline` and `e2-trestle` again. 📜 **THE CHAIN, EACH LINK VERIFIED BY READING THE COMMIT, NOT THE ROW:** the ruling shipped as `f1605-1` at **`88530e3ef`** (authored s1605, drained s1606, review `reviews/f1605-1-e2s3-door-delist.md`), which de-listed the three from `SUPPORTED_CONTRACTS` and **deliberately left the escort-mode arm intact** so escort callers were untouched. Then **`48a0d41ab`** (the `ap16-4-same-game-admission` runner commit, 2026-08-11T00:02, `git merge-base --is-ancestor` → on main) replaced the hand-maintained literal with a derivation — registry minus a new `CONTRACT_ADMISSION_EXEMPTIONS` table. **The four E5/E6 refusals and `e3-fairground` were carried across as cited entries; the three E2 railcars were not**, so the derivation swept them back in. 🔑 **THE ROOT IS ONE SENTENCE OF ARITHMETIC IN THE AP-16-4 MASTER,