rted lines, which is the tell. I had inferred the `—`-escaping convention from the *titles* — written by an older serializer — and generalised it to a file that no longer obeys it. **Narrowed the denominator to the text I generate**, which is the only thing a splice can be responsible for. Same family as the guard-denominator findings: a check whose subject is wider than its author's change reports other people's history as your defect. 📁 Splice script retained in-repo per the RETENTION LAW (`scripts/tmp-s1664-price-leaves.mjs`); it refuses on a missing/duplicate id, a pre-existing block, non-ASCII in its own output, and any parse or tree-shape change outside `authoringBlock`.
🟢 **F-1654-1 (s1654 2026-08-11, MEASURED + CURED THIS FIRE — THE FOURTH CONSECUTIVE FIRE TO PROVE THE SAME NEGATIVES, AND THE REASON IS THAT A MEASURED REFUSAL HAD NOWHERE TO LIVE. NOT AN OWNER QUESTION.)** 📋 **THE RUN, and F-1653-2 already named it: s1641 (F-1641-3, three `planned` leaves with no spec slice) · s1649 (F-1649-1, AP-16-6) · s1650 (F-1650-1, AP-03) · s1653 (F-1653-2, AP-15 slice 2).** Each measured a refusal correctly, wrote it as a BACKLOG *finding*, and left the surface a refilling fire actually reads carrying **nothing**. The next fire then re-derived it from scratch. 🎯 **F-1653-2 PRESCRIBED THE CURE AT THE WRONG SURFACE, AND I CHECKED BEFORE SPENDING THE BUDGET IT ASKED FOR.** It says every owner-gated or already-shipped rung *"should say so **in the row**, so a refilling fire pays one grep instead of one whole budget"* — but **none of the three rungs HAS a BACKLOG ladder row.** Measured: `ap16-6-action-verbs` appears only in `specs/agent-play/ap-16-same-game-law.md:35` and as a `tasks/goals.json` leaf; `ap-03-protocol` and `ap-15-assay-of-minds` likewise carry no `- ` ladder row naming them as authorable work. **The rungs live as `status:"planned"` GOAL LEAVES.** Marking rows that do not exist would have cured nothing and read as done. 🔬 **AND BOTH EXISTING INSTRUMENTS ARE BLIND HERE BY CONSTRUCTION — I checked rather than built first (the "the SAME FILE may already solve it" rule).** `scripts/drain-block-check.mjs` resolves `blocked`/`stopped` leaves across 27 spellings and contains **zero** occurrences of the string `planned` — correctly, because **a refill question is not a drain question**; §3.0's block asks *may I MERGE this*, not *may I AUTHOR this*. `scripts/ghost-ladder-row-guard.mjs` keys on lead-📋 rows that name a **master file path** (`tasks/*.md`) and classifies it SHIPPED — an unauthored rung has no master, so it can never match. Neither is defective; the question simply had no owner. 📊 **THE CENSUS, and it is the number that makes this cheap to fix: the factory's ENTIRE authorable-candidate surface is TWELVE `planned` leaves** (against 666 `merged` / 57 `shipped` / 25 `superseded` / 11 `verified-by-owner` / 5 `building` / 5 `stopped` / 3 `blocked`). **Before this fire: 2 priced, 10 unpriced.** Four fires each burned an authoring budget choosing among twelve rows, none of which recorded what the last fire learned. ✅ **CURED, in the leaf and in an instrument.** (1) The three already-paid measurements are transcribed onto their leaves as a structured `authoringBlock` {class · finding · measuredBy · reason} — `ap16-6-action-verbs` ← F-1649-1, `ap-03-protocol` ← F-1650-1, `ap-15-assay-of-minds` ← F-1653-2. Spliced, never re-serialized: **21 insertions, 3 deletions** (the three `status` lines gaining a comma). (2) `scripts/authorable-candidates.mjs` lists all twelve with their class and citation in one command; **advisory, exit 0** by the `drain-block-check` UNKNOWN precedent — `--strict` is opt-in, because 7 unpriced legacy leaves would otherwise red the whole board rather than answer the question asked. (3) `scripts/authorable-candidates.test.mjs`, **10 tests, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`**, each red path proven by **manufacturing the defect** on fixtures (unpriced leaf → `--strict` rc=1; a typo'd class `owner-frok` → degraded to `unclassified` and *said so* rather than trusted; an `authoringBlock` with no `reason` → does NOT read as priced). ⚖️ **READ THE CLASS, NOT JUST THE PRICE — this is F-1383-1's discriminator moved from draining to authoring, and it is the half that decides who is owed.** Of the three: **`ap-15-assay-of-minds` is OWNER-GATED** (3 open ratification questions — it belongs on the desk, and F-1653-2 already has it there); **`ap16-6-action-verbs` and `ap-03-protocol` are ATTENDED-OWED** — no owner word will ever lift them, so carrying them to the desk would park them forever, exactly as a `gate-side` block carried as `owner-fork` does. 📉 **STATE AFTER: 5 priced (1 owner-gated · 2 attended-owed · 2 prose-only) / 7 unpriced.** ⚠️ **I DELIBERATELY DID NOT INVENT VERDICTS FOR THE OTHER SEVEN** — `rf-04-bounty` · `rf-05-fixed-version` · `stream-live` · `sea-3-season1-content` · `ap-04-teach` · `ap-05-publish` · `foundry-first-real-game`. Pricing a leaf I have not measured is the precise failure this finding is about, one level up. ⓘ **ONE LEAD FOR THE NEXT FIRE, OFFERED AS AN INFERENCE AND LABELLED AS ONE:** `ap-04-teach` and `ap-05-publish` both carry *"SAME CONJUNCTIVE GATE AS AP-03"* in their own titles, so F-1650-1's measurement may well decide them too — **but I did not open their surfaces, so that is a hypothesis, not a price.** 💡 **THE REUSABLE HALF, and it is not the one F-1653-2 expected: a finding's prescribed cure can name a surface that does not exist, and the prescription is written by the fire that had just finished measuring — the moment it is most trusted.** F-1653-2's diagnosis was exactly right and its cure was aimed one surface off. Checking that the surface exists cost one `grep` and saved the whole budget it asked for; F-1310-1's *cite by CONTENT, not coordinate* generalises — **verify the TARGET of a cure the way you would verify a citation.**
