ir of surfaces (F-1279-1: a ruling recorded in BACKLOG while `goals.json` kept refusing). **It checks ONE DIRECTION** — leaves that still refuse while BACKLOG says RULED. Here the leaves were correctly freed and **BACKLOG kept refusing**, so the guard is structurally incapable of seeing it: run this fire it reports **`3 findings recorded RULED · 29 goal leaves still refuse work · 0 stale · PASS`**. ⓘ **A SECOND, INDEPENDENT GAP, measured while checking the first: the guard's own vocabulary has fallen behind the practice its header told it to track.** Its regex is `/\b(F-\d+-\d+)\s+RULED\b/` — **uppercase-only, digits-only ids** — while roundup #2 writes *"ruled"* in lowercase and uses slug ids. **Counted across `tasks/BACKLOG.md`: 10 findings are recorded ruled in some case; the guard's vocabulary sees 3.** Missed: `F-1493-3`, `F-1167-1`, `F-1193-3`, `F-E2S-3`, `F-1415-5`, `F-1392-3`. Its header says in as many words *"Widen the vocabulary only when the practice widens it"* — **the practice widened on 2026-08-09 and the widening event is the very commit this finding is about.** 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT CURED BY MECHANISM THIS FIRE, and the restraint is the point (F-1594-1 / F-1613-2 precedent — two proposed guards refuted by measuring them before building them).** Widening the regex only improves the direction that is already **0 stale**; the direction that actually bit us is unchecked entirely, and checking it means parsing `GATE:` prose in BACKLOG — a judgement surface, which is how a guard earns a permanent excused red (the `cross-engine` fate, F-1460-1). **Anyone building it must measure its precision against these three known instances FIRST.** ✅ **CURED BY LEDGER THIS FIRE:** all three rows carry a dated `RULED` clause with the ruling quoted verbatim and a **restated GATE naming the true residual act and its ACTOR** — fairground is owed by the **attended session** (not the owner), bt-04 is unblocked as a **program** but still missing its four **parameters**, and F