🟢 **F-1613-1 (s1613 2026-08-10, MEASURED BY TESTING THE REPAIR INSTEAD OF APPLYING IT — THE GZ-01 RETRO-MARK'S BLANK LINE IS LOAD-BEARING, AND THE OBVIOUS EDITORIAL FIX SILENTLY SWEEPS A PUBLISHED NEWS ITEM INTO `dismissed`).** Non-blocking, **no code owed**, cure already applied this drain. 🔎 **HOW IT SURFACED:** gating `f1612-1` I saw the marker had been inserted at `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md:1266` **with a blank line above it**, severing a sentence mid-clause — the published note now reads *"…the same pass turned up six"* / *"NOT PLAYER-VISIBLE uncited merges and four were judged NOT player-visible…"*. The master had said in terms **do not re-flow that note** (published owner-facing prose), so my first reading was a firewall violation in the one file where it would reach a human. ✓ **THAT READING IS WRONG, AND I ONLY KNOW BECAUSE I TESTED THE REPAIR RATHER THAN MAKING IT.** The roundup's own two **reported** hashes (`ba78dad5e`, `88530e3ef`) share one contiguous run of prose with the four dismissed ones, and paragraph scope cannot tell them apart — **the blank line is the ONLY thing scoping the marker to the four.** Applying the tidy repair in the gate worktree (un-split the sentence, marker appended at the paragraph end) and re-running the sweep: **reported 62 / dismissed 9 / candidates 0** — five extra merges swept into `dismissed`, including **`88530e3ef`, which that very roundup PUBLISHES AS NEWS**, plus `c742cd596` and `ba78dad5e`. ⚠️ **THE TRAP IS WELL-SHAPED FOR THIS FACTORY AND THAT IS WHY IT EARNS A ROW: the damage looks like a typo, the repair looks like tidying, and NOTHING WILL RED.** The sweep is advisory and **exits 0 in every state** by law (F-1600-1 bars a red guard here because player-visibility is a judgement), and `classifyCitation`'s test is **fixture-driven by design** — the master required that, precisely so it would not go stale every time a fire publishes — so it is structurally incapable of seeing the live board. A future fire fix