🟢 **F-1613-2 (s1613 2026-08-10, A NEGATIVE RESULT THAT ANSWERS F-1594-1'S ONE OPEN RECOMMENDATION — THE "NARROW ARM" IS NOT MECHANISABLE EITHER, AND I KNOW BECAUSE I RAN IT BEFORE AUTHORING IT).** Non-blocking, no code owed, **two real ledger defects found and cured in the same act.** 🔎 **WHY I RAN IT AT ALL:** the board went dry after my drain with four idle lanes, and [F-1594-1] carries the only standing invitation on the ladder — it declined to mechanise its class *"because cross-row causality is a judgement"* but named an exception: *"what WOULD be mechanisable, IF THIS RECURS, is the NARROW ARM only: a row whose header contains `OPEN`/`FIRE-AUTHORABLE` or a bare `🔧`, and whose body contains a merge hash that `git merge-base --is-ancestor` places on main. That arm is a FACT, not a judgement."* Its own precision figure was **1 false positive in 3 hits**. ✓ **SO I IMPLEMENTED THE ARM AS A THROWAWAY PROBE AND MEASURED IT ON THE LIVE BOARD RATHER THAN AUTHORING A MASTER FROM THE RECOMMENDATION.** 📊 **RESULT — 20 hits, of which 8 already carry a `⛔` banner IN THE HEADER and 9 more carry a closure in the tail; only 3 are neither, and all 3 are legitimately open** (`F-1599-1` doc-only OPEN, `F-1193-3` on the owner's desk, and a STOPPED-lane note — none of them queueable masters). **Precision on "would re-queue shipped work": 0 of 20 after the two cures below; the arm reds on 17 correctly-written rows.** That is a **>50% false-positive rate on a board that is behaving**, far worse than the 1-in-3 that already persuaded s1594 to decline — and an excused red is worse than no test (F-1460-1, measured). 🚫 **THEREFORE THE RECOMMENDATION IS CLOSED AS REFUTED, NOT DEFERRED. Do not author this guard.** ⚠️ **AND THE ARM MISSED A GENUINE INSTANCE, WHICH IS THE HALF THAT SETTLES IT:** `f1607-1` (L22) is exactly the defect the arm exists to catch — merged `0b062962e`, bare `🔧 … AUTHORED` header — and it **did not appear in the 20 hits at all**, because the hash forms in its body did not satisfy the matcher. A guard with ~15% precision **and** a false negative on the very class it was drawn from is not a guard, it is noise with a citation. 💡 **The reusable half: F-1594-1's arm was described as "a FACT, not a judgement", and that is TRUE and still not sufficient — a fact-shaped predicate can be perfectly well-defined and still land almost entirely on rows that are already correct, because what makes those rows correct (a `⛔` banner, a tail closure) is invisible to it. Cheap discriminator: implement the predicate as a scratch probe and count its hits against the live corpus BEFORE writing a master for it.** That cost one command and saved a lane run plus a permanent red. 🔧 **THE TWO REAL DEFECTS, CURED THIS FIRE (banner convention, F-1594-1's own prescribed standing defence):** `f1608-1` (L21, merged `6c780b621`) and `f1607-1` (L22, merged `0b062962e`) both kept bare `🔧 … AUTHORED` ladder headers while their work shipped, because each closure was written into a **neighbouring row** (`F-1493-3 DISCHARGED` sits three rows above f1607-1's). A dry-board audit scanning ladder headers for refillable work could have re-queued a shipped ART batch and a shipped balance master — **Mistake #8, The 824k Flail, exactly.** Each was verified by **three independent probes** before the banner: `merge-base --is-ancestor`, the `drained-<hash>-` done-move, and a `merged` goal leaf carrying that hash — never a message-grep (Mistake #16). **GATE: none owed — no owner word, no code. This row closes F-1594-1's narrow-arm recommendation with a measurement; the standing defence remains the banner convention plus `/author-task`.** Related: [F-1594-1], [F-1593-3], [F-1460-1], [F-1556-1].
