/nul-audit.mjs` then named it at offset 2921. Cured by constructing the NUL with `String.fromCharCode(0)` in a fix script rather than typing one (a file that types the character to fix the character re-introduces it); `nul-audit` now reads **CLEAN**. ⓘ The guard already existed and would have reddened at `test:ledger-guards`, my last act — so the mechanism worked; what nearly failed was noticing an hour earlier. ⚠️ **THEN IT HAPPENED A SECOND TIME, IN THE COMMIT WRITING THIS VERY WARNING** — quoting the offending phrase back into the row to explain it re-wrote the byte, and `nul-audit` caught it again within the minute. **That is the actual lesson, and it is not carelessness: any prose that QUOTES the character re-introduces it, so the hazard is a property of writing about NULs at all.** ➡️ Therefore: never paste the literal to describe it — write the six-character escape, and run `node scripts/nul-audit.mjs` after any ledger edit that so much as mentions delimiters.
