260:🟢 **F-1600-1** (s1600 2026-08-09, MEASURED AND CURED THIS FIRE, DOC-ONLY — THE GAZETTE SWEEP’S HASH CHECK IS STRUCTURALLY BLIND TO THE SECOND OWNER-FACING SINK, SO 44.7% OF ITS “ABSENT” VERDICTS ARE ITEMS THE OWNER HAS ALREADY BEEN SHOWN). Found while discharging s1599’s deliberately-deferred (B). ⚠️ **THE SENTENCE THIS REFUTES IS A PRIOR FINDING’S EXONERATION.** F-1593-1 audited this very sweep, split it into halves, and wrote *“the hash half is a `grep` and cannot go wrong; the ‘real-change’ half needs the merge’s file list”* — then spent its entire investigation on the second half. **The hash half went wrong in two independent ways, and that exoneration is why nobody looked.** 🔑 **THE MECHANISM:** the news pipeline has TWO owner-facing sinks — GAZETTE items in `marketing/outbox/gazette-queue.md` and the daily TK-01 ticker digests sitting beside it — and the duty’s prescribed check greps ONE file for the FULL 40-char hash. 📐 **The two sinks cite hashes in DISJOINT conventions, which makes the blindness categorical rather than a sampling artifact — ✓ VERIFIED by counting every hash-shaped token in the live outbox: ticker digests carry 618 short hashes and ZERO full-40 ones; `gazette-queue.md` carries 86 full and 105 short.** A full-40 grep therefore **cannot** match a ticker digest in principle, however many fires run it. 📊 **MEASURED (`scripts/tmp-s1600-outbox-sinks.mjs`, window 2026-08-05→s1600): 1065 first-parent commits, 81 touching player paths (`src/` `functions/` `public/` `index.html` `e2e/`), of which the narrow check calls 47 ABSENT — but 20 are headlined in a ticker digest and 1 sits in the gazette under its short hash. So 21 of 47 are FALSE POSITIVES (44.7%), and only 26 are genuinely unreported.** ⚠️ **My denominator is NOT s1599’s, and I do not claim to have re-priced its exact figures:** s1599 filtered on commit-message prefix (53 shaped / 37 absent); I filtered on touched paths (81 / 47). **The transferable result is the RATE, not the count.** ⓘ **THE DAMAGE IS AN ITEM THAT CAN NEVER BE DISCHARGED, NOT WASTED GREPS:** `3b2b33c29` (“the county’s first standing — V4 Pro secures the-claim via the public door”) was left by s1599 as an UNJUDGED gazette candidate and re-judged by me — when it had been headlined to the owner in `ticker-digest-2026-08-06.md:27–29` on 2026-08-07, **carrying its own OWNER CHOICE note at `:58`**, since before either fire existed. A check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again; this one was on its third pass. ✅ **VERDICT ON THAT CANDIDATE, so it stops circulating: REPORTED, NOT OWED — no gazette item, and it was never a real-change merge anyway** (its diff is `logs/seed-ladder/`, two run transcripts, `scripts/seed-ladder.mjs` +5/-1, `tasks/BACKLOG.md` +1 — no `src/`, no `functions/`). 💡 **THIS REPRICES ANY ABSENCE COUNT TAKEN THE NARROW WAY, INCLUDING F-1599-1’S** — if ~45% of such a set is already published, the backlog it implies is smaller than it reads, and a cure sized against the raw figure is over-sized. ⚖️ **BUT IT DOES NOT REFUTE F-1599-1, AND I CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED:** its instance `a97ff79c7` appears in the outbox today **only because s1599 backfilled it by hand** (`0760e05da`); re-greped at both hash lengths, **no ticker digest ever carried it**, so F-1599-1 was a TRUE miss and not an artifact of this defect. My finding changes the SIZE of that problem, not its existence. ✅ **CURED IN `scripts/fire.md` GZ-01 THIS FIRE:** the check is now “grep the 8-char SHORT hash across the whole of `marketing/outbox/`”. Doc-only, no code, no new guard — the duty’s own standing prohibition on mechanising this as a red guard is untouched and still right. **GATE: none — closed on landing. Reverse with one word if the owner prefers the narrow check.** ✅ **SWEEP DISCHARGED THIS FIRE WITH THE CORRECTED CHECK, WHICH IS HOW THE REST OF THIS ROW WAS LEARNED.** Of the 47 the narrow check called absent, **4** touch real player source once `e2e/` is dropped from the filter (a test is not a player-facing surface), and **3 of those 4 are genuine misses** — backfilled as one ROUNDUP per the ≤3/week rule: `c8807b4d` (THE FRONT DESK panel beside the county boards — `renderFrontDesk()` + 99 lines of `reader.css`), `7e5fae14` (the e2-trestle terrain rebuild, `Terrain3dClaimPilot.ts` +243 with new atlas/blend/glb), `d9cf6242` (a works with power lines but no connection to make would pin `objectiveAllowsSecure` false forever, so beating the Baron **won the contract and silently failed to secure it**). The 4th, `1a2871fd`, is factory hygiene (composite-key delimiters re-encoded so `grep` works in Claude shells) and is CORRECTLY absent. 🔎 **A THIRD BLINDNESS, found only by discharging the duty rather than measuring it — AND IT IS Mistake #16 SITTING INSIDE THE SWEEP’S OWN FILTER.** s1599 shaped its candidate set by commit-MESSAGE PREFIX (`fix|feat|perf|test|refactor`). **Two of my three genuine misses land under subjects that name something else entirely:** `c8807b4d` ships a whole new player-facing panel under *“bench: prime-agent heat 1 closes DNF×3 (operability trilogy)”*, and `7e5fae14` is a bare *“Merge branch ‘lane/c’ into HEAD”*. **A message-prefix filter cannot see either, and no amount of widening the sink fixes that** — it is the same law the house already wrote after w1-07 (never judge shipped-ness by commit messages), reappearing in the instrument that judges newsworthiness. ➡️ **Shape the candidate set by TOUCHED PATHS, never by subject.** 📐 **The trestle miss also has a sibling control, which is what raised it from “arguably” to “owed”:** `beauty-e2-pressure-garden` (`25890bae…`) and `beauty-e2-incline` (`fa5ed7ca…`) both carry gazette items; the trestle pass is the same class of work by the same hands and had none. Two of three announced is not a judgement call, it is a gap.
