nes` (all `z ∈ [36,46]`), while `west-fog-pocket` tops out at `z ≤ 18` and `ridge-dead-gap` needs a 40 wu span that `Balance.e7Signal.linkRange = 28` rejects one line EARLIER (`E7SignalSystem.ts:222` `continue`s on range before the fog test at `:223`). ⇒ **every link decision on this map is made by Euclidean distance alone; "relays connect only when they can see one another" is scenery.** Socketing it would assert a Signal playability that does not exist — **precisely the `e3-fairground` refusal shape F-1481-2 names as the honest discriminator.** 🟩 **`e9-dome-basin` — SOCKETABLE, and the cheapest real socket left.** All three stated objectives (ice quarry · stage-gates C1/C2/C3 · dust-devil lane) are owned by **one class**, `E9CanalSystem`, which is **DOM-free** (a grep for `document|window|localStorage|Math.random|Date.now|randomUUID` across the six candidate systems hits only `E7SignalSystem.ts:92,104,206` and `OldDiggerBossSystem.ts:627` — *not* E9Canal), deterministic in `(delta, at, actors)`, and its `Actor` type `{position, speed}` is **already what `HeadlessContractSim.harvestTargets()` produces**. It does hide two gaps (`OldDiggerBossSystem`, `E9ArsenalSystem`) — but declaring them IS the F-1480-2 cure, and neither needs new gameplay, which is the load-bearing discriminator separating socket work from the owner-forked ten. ⚖️ **STATED HONESTLY: under F-1481-2's BARE WORDS (*"if it finds one the contract collapses"*) dome-basin collapses too. That literal reading would also have collapsed `e2-hill-mine` before its socket landed — i.e. it would forbid the very template this ladder is built on.** The substantive test is new-gameplay-vs-socket-work; a fire should not adopt the literal one without an attended word, so this is flagged, not silently overridden. 💣 **LANDMINES BANKED FOR WHOEVER AUTHORS IT** (each measured, not guessed): `scripts/gr-sim.mjs:15` shims only `location`+`window` — **no `document`, no `localStorage`** · the dome-basin analogue of the `cry