633:- 🔺 **F-1485-1 (s1485, MEASURED — F-1470-4's 301 HELD CELLS ARE THREE CLASSES WITH THREE DIFFERENT CURES, AND THE 45-CELL ROUNDED-SCALE CLASS IS BLOCKED BY A TOOLING DEFECT, NOT BY ART.)** 🧭 **HOW I FOUND IT:** the board was dry and s1484 ranked F-1470-4 first, so before authoring anything I ran the gate's own predicate against the live corpus (F-1483-1). The row reads as one 301-cell blob whose members all "revert shipped mends or move the silhouette". **Measured, it is not.** 📐 **THE SPLIT (`artifacts/f1470-4/*`, all tracked and re-derivable in one command each):** **(A) 64 cells / 2 sheets** — `char-{baron,hero}-sheet-walk8`, the cutout-pocket fork that failed closed; genuinely eye-gated, UNCHANGED by this fire. **(B) 192 cells / 6 sheets** — the unledgered direct-output mend sheets, all `scale == 1`; UNCHANGED, not probed. **(C) 45 cells / 7 sheets** — the rounded-scale class, and the whole of this finding. 🔑 **THE DEFECT, NAMED IN CODE RATHER THAN INFERRED:** `extract-alpha.mjs:376` computes `scale = min(1, (cell * 0.86) / maxDim)` as a full double, `:412` writes it to `frames.json` as `Number(scale.toFixed(4))`, and `anim-pass-reextract.mjs:163` reads that **4dp** value back out and passes it in as `--scale`. Every re-extraction is therefore normalised at a scale wrong in the 5th decimal, resampling every cell a hair differently — which is exactly the alpha drift the strict invariant caught. ⚠️ **Sheets whose scale clamps to 1 are IMMUNE, because `min(1, …)` makes the rounding unobservable — and those are precisely the 774 that passed. The bug was invisible across 94% of the corpus by arithmetic accident, not because the pipeline was right.** ✅ **THE CURE, MEASURED END-TO-END ON ALL 45 CELLS (`artifacts/f1470-4/exact-scale-recipe.mjs`):** `maxDim` is an integer pixel count, so the original double is recoverable exactly — `maxDim = round(cell * 0.86 / shippedScale)`, then `scale = cell * 0.86 / maxDim`. Result across 7 sheets / 45 cells: **halo suspects 45 → 0 · alpha differences 0 (the silhouette provably does not move) · 117 fully-opaque pixels change RGB, every one of them by exactly 1/255.** 🚫 **THE OBVIOUS FIX IS WRONG, AND MEASURING IT IS WHAT SAVED THE RECIPE:** simply dropping `--scale` and letting the extractor auto-fit reproduces 4 sheets exactly and is **badly wrong on 3** — the halo cure shrinks the content bbox, so the auto-fit recomputes `maxDim` and renormalises the figure. `char-hero-sheet-rotation2-f` would go **0.7644 → 0.8719, drawing the hero ~14% larger than her sibling sheets**, with alpha deltas up to 255. *The auto path silently changes sprite SIZE; the recovery recipe does not.* 🔬 **INSTRUMENT VALIDATED BEFORE ITS NUMBERS WERE BELIEVED (`artifacts/f1470-4/instrument-controls.mjs`), because a green here proves nothing about a red:** control 1 — my sweep predicate reads **45/45** shipped rounded-scale cells as >5% suspects and **disagrees with the tracked sweep on 0**; control 2 — the same extract+resize+compare pipeline run against three **already-cured** sheets returns **alphaDiff 0 / opaqueRGB 0**, exactly, so the residue it reports on the held sheets belongs to the sprite and not to my reproduction. The A/B's **control arm reproduces the runner's failure** on all 7 sheets, so the hypothesis arm was measured against a known-bad baseline, not against nothing. 🔎 **AND ONE INHERITED CLAIM IS CORRECTED:** the f1464-1 master's measured note 2 states that of the RGB pixels the cure changes, **"0 are fully opaque"**. That was measured on **one sheet** (`char-baron-sheet-walk4-a`) and does not generalise — the cure moves **41 fully-opaque master pixels** across these 23 cells. It moves each by **exactly 1**, so the note's *spirit* (the interior does not move) survives intact and its *letter* does not. **A claim that is true for a reason its author never checked is still an unverified claim.** ⚖️ **WHY THIS FIRE STOPPED HERE AND AUTHORED NO MASTER:** the recipe satisfies every clause of F-1470-4's first disjunct except **"byte-identical … opaque RGB"**, which 117 pixels violate by 1/255. The f1464-1 master says in as many words that a failure of that invariant *"is a FINDING with the file named — not a threshold to relax"*, and **a fire may not relax a threshold an owner-facing gate is written on.** Running the predicate first is what revealed that a master queued today would fail its own acceptance gate — the F-1483-1 lesson, paying for itself before any tokens were spent on scope. **GATE: closes on ONE WORD — is an opaque-RGB delta of ≤1/255 acceptable when alpha is byte-identical? YES ⇒ 45 of the 301 cells are curable by a fire-authored master in a single lane shift, and (A)+(B)'s 256 cells remain the honest residue. NO ⇒ class (C) joins them at the attended eye, and this row closes as measured-and-declined.** 🚫 Do NOT "fix" this by editing `scripts/extract-alpha.mjs` — the 4dp record is what 1,314 shipped `frames.json` files already contain, and widening it would strand the recovery arithmetic that reads them.
