993:🟡 **F-1383-2 (s1383, MEASURED — "THE CHEAPEST REAL WORK ON THE BOARD" IS NOT A TEST REPAIR, AND IT LEADS STRAIGHT INTO A BLOCKED LEAF. DO NOT AUTHOR IT AS A SCOPED FIXTURE FIX.)** s1380 filed F-1380-2 and called it *"the cheapest real work on the board"*; s1381 repeated that. I verified the subject before authoring a master against it (**a measurement task must verify its subject is present**) and the framing does not survive contact. ✓ **STILL RED, both projects, re-measured s1383 at `--workers=1`** — but **it fails at `e2e/agent-view.spec.ts:266`, the `expect(ids).toEqual([...])` list, NOT at `:267` where the fixture comparison lives.** The live family is **SIX** contracts — `["the-claim","e1-drill-yard","e1-dry-gulch","e1-night-shift","e1-twin-banks","e1-baron"]` — while the test hardcodes **five** and omits `e1-drill-yard`; **the test's own title still says "all five"**, so the title is a stale claim too. ⇒ **The early assertion DISABLES everything after it: `expect(manifests).toEqual(fixtures)` and the byte-stability compare have not executed at all.** Calling this a fixture-drift repair mis-states which assertion is broken and hides that the fixture oracle is **dark**, not failing. 🔗 **AND REPAIRING `:266` WALKS DIRECTLY INTO A BLOCKED LEAF.** `f1328-1-drill-yard-census-debt` (now **`blockClass: "disputed"`** per F-1383-1) is about **exactly this subject**: *"deriveMechanicsManifest(\"e1-drill-yard\") returns interactables:[] and rules river/water_crossings despite the yard declaring a bell, dummies, practice gold and buildables — the derivation ignores `practice`, an AP-11 NO-UNDECLARED-MECHANICS violation AT THE DERIVATION."* Adding `e1-drill-yard` to the id list makes the next two assertions compare that derivation against the fixture — which is precisely the **JUDGEMENT its leaf reserves**: *"does a byte-stable fixture of F-1328-4's wrong derivation bless it or catch it?"* That leaf also records **two dispatches already** and *"THIRD ATTEMPT REQUIRES A CHANGED PREMISE per the twice-then-escalate law."* 🚫 **THEREFORE: NOT fire-authorable as written, and this is why s1383 authored NO refill master despite two USABLE lanes.** Inventing a scoped test repair here would have been the [do-not-touch list contains the blocker] shape — the cheap-looking half is load-bearing on the reserved half. ➡️ **RECOMMENDATION (needs no owner word): the changed premise the leaf asks for is option (a) — fix the DERIVATION in its own slice first** (`practice` declarations must reach `deriveMechanicsManifest`), **then** the id list, title and fixture all follow mechanically and the byte-stable oracle lights up for the first time. That ordering also converts the disputed leaf's judgement question into a moot one, because the fixture would then bless a *correct* derivation. 💡 **The reusable half: when an inherited finding says "cheapest work on the board", re-measure WHICH ASSERTION FAILS before believing the scope. A red attributed to the assertion it is NAMED after, rather than the one that actually threw, will size the job wrong every time — and here it also concealed that a second, more expensive question was sitting one line below it.**
1015:🟢 **F-1378-1 (s1378, MEASURED + LANDED SAME FIRE — THE FOURTH RECORDED INSTANCE OF THE MISAPPLIED-OWNER-GATE CLASS, AND THIS TIME THE CITED AUTHORITY WAS QUOTED THREE TIMES WITHOUT ANYONE OPENING IT. THREE FILED DOC CURES SAT ON THE OWNER'S DESK FOR THREE FIRES BEHIND A PROHIBITION THAT DOES NOT EXIST.)** 🧭 **THE PROBE.** s1377 §K(3) handed forward no hypothesis and prescribed the shape: verify the duties, take ONE bounded question, STOP. The desk carried an item unchanged since s1374 — *"THREE SMALLEST-THINGS-ON-THE-DESK, ALL IN-LINE DOC SUBSTITUTIONS, ~80 SECONDS TOTAL"*. **An 80-second act that has waited three fires is either mislabelled or misunderstood**, and this ledger already records the class firing three times (F-1271-1 *"the act s1270 sent to the owner's desk was NEVER owner-gated"*, F-1335-6, F-1350-1 *"the OWNER'S DESK label overrode [its own unblocking instruction] for NINETEEN fires"*). I did not ask *should these land?* — I asked **what exactly forbids a fire from landing them, and where is it written?** ⚠️ **THE ANSWER: NOWHERE.** All three rows give the same reason — F-1374-1: *"because it edits THE CONSTITUTION, I am filing it rather than landing it (§7.7: don't rewrite law surfaces unilaterally)"*; F-1375-1 and F-1376-1: *"`fire.md` is the fire protocol's own constitution and §7.7 plus the standing order forbid drive-by edits to it."* **§7.7 read at source (`CLAUDE.md:71`) says:** *"You're about to do something irreversible (force-push [denied anyway], deleting branches, rewriting a ratified spec's rulings) → don't."* Three named acts, all irreversible or ruling-changing. **A reversible in-line character substitution correcting a MEASURED-STALE fact is none of them** — and the parenthetical gloss *"don't rewrite law surfaces unilaterally"* appears in F-1374-1's row, **not in §7.7**. 🎯 **AND THE CLAUSE THAT DOES APPLY POINTS THE OTHER WAY, THREE LINES ABOVE IT.** `CLAUDE.md:68` §7.4: *"**Owner absent + action reversible + inside ratified specs** → proceed, and write a veto-window line in the handoff."* Owner absent ✓, reversible ✓ (a commit), inside ratified law ✓ (each edit makes the law state what it already means). **§7.4 does not merely permit these three — it prescribes exactly how to do them, and the veto-window line is the price.** Paid in this fire's handoff. 📐 **THE DENOMINATOR, RE-DERIVED NOT INHERITED (Mistake #4).** Swept all six law surfaces (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `scripts/fire.md`, the three `.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md`) for any prohibition on a fire editing a law surface: **ZERO**. The only "drive-by" ban in the corpus is `scripts/fire.md:13`, and it is scoped to **the timestamp LABEL** (*"fix the label only as a deliberate flag-day landing in every fire at once — never as a drive-by"*), not to the file. The other standing order, carried verbatim through 11 handoff archives, is *"do not drive-by-edit fire.md's TWICE"* — **ONE WORD** in `CLAUDE.md` §10b, a deliberate historical count. **Neither generalises to the file, and both were read as if they did.** 🔬 **THE PRACTICE REFUTES IT TOO, WHICH IS THE HALF THAT SETTLES IT.** `git log` on the two surfaces: **`scripts/fire.md` 20 of 26 commits carry an `sNNNN:` fire prefix; `CLAUDE.md` 6 of 10.** Fires are the PRIMARY authors of both. Two are decisive: **`ebda186f` "s1276: correct two law surfaces that stated what their own code had stopped doing"** — a fire, both files, *this exact defect class* — and **`b007cbc6` "s1342: correct my own denominator — 140 s9 bullets is 18 law bullets + 119 handoff archives"**, a fire editing **the very §3.0b sentence** that F-1375-1 three fires later declined to touch. ⭐ **And the law says so in its own voice: `scripts/fire.md:23` (F-1300-4) states that "a fire mutates three such subjects: ledger rows, **law surfaces** (`scripts/fire.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills/**`)… and gate topology"** — the mandatory post-bookkeeping battery exists *because* fires edit these files. **The prohibition was inferred from a battery built on the opposite premise.** ✅ **LANDED, ALL THREE (`7a2780be`), each re-verified at source before it was applied — never inherited.** **F-1374-1** `CLAUDE.md` §10b `v2:76/**v3:152**` → `lane-runner-v2.sh:76/**lane-runner-v3.sh:152**`; both lines READ at source first and both are verbatim the `.git/*.stale*`+`tmp_obj_*` sweep the sentence claims. **The cure works precisely as predicted and the guard proves it: `law-pointer-guard` went 23 → 25 pointers (checked 20 → 22), FAILED with two `NEW POINTER` entries demanding eyeball confirmation, then PASSED after `--update`.** Two live law coordinates that were unguarded this morning are guarded tonight, with no widened regex and no new mechanism — exactly the resolution path F-1374-1 predicted via `resolveCited`'s basename fallback. **F-1375-1** `fire.md` §3.0b: the 3 bare `- **s9 ` VM-era env bullets now named, so the census reads 18 + 119 + 3 = 140 instead of a 137 that claimed to be 140. **F-1376-1** `fire.md:23`: *"those **eight** and nothing else — **36 tests**"* → **eleven guards / 12 leaf files / 38 tests**, plus an explicit *"COUNT it, never PRUNE it back to the number written here"*. Numbers re-derived, not inherited: `package.json` resolved by hand to 12 components, battery **rc=0, 38 tests / 38 pass / 0 fail** both before and after my edits. 🪤 **A FOURTH DEFECT FELL OUT OF LANDING RATHER THAN READING, AND IT IS THE SHARPEST THING HERE: F-1376-1'S FILED CURE TEXT MATCHED *ZERO* OCCURRENCES OF THE FILE.** It prescribed substituting `is now those **eight** and nothing else — **36 tests**, seconds` — but `fire.md` bolds the whole clause: `— **36 tests, seconds, not a second battery.**`. **A future attended session applying the filed text literally would have found nothing to replace.** This is the standing lesson *a cure written by someone who could not run it is untested* — sharpened, because s1376 **could** have run it and chose to file. **Filing does not preserve a cure; it preserves an UNTESTED DRAFT of one, and the draft decays against the file it was never matched to.** ⓘ **HONEST SCOPE — WHAT I AM *NOT* CLAIMING.** I am not claiming fires may edit any law surface at will. `.claude/**` **is** genuinely gated — a real, mechanical, twice-tested denial (F-1343-1, re-tested F-1349-1: *"still denied, and NO settings change can lift it… Do NOT shell around it"*), which is why `001-drain-skill-custody-rule.md` sits **correctly** in `attended-owed-audit` and I left it there. **That contrast is the finding's spine: this factory has one real gate on law surfaces and one imagined one, and only the real one has a mechanism.** A gate you can name twenty commits that violated is not a gate. 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE.** s1374: ask what the guard that owns a claim cannot reach. s1375: measure what widening would sweep IN. s1376: a law that states a set's SIZE freezes a set it commands to grow. **s1378: A CITED AUTHORITY IS A CLAIM LIKE ANY OTHER — OPEN IT. Three fires quoted "§7.7" and none of them read `CLAUDE.md:71`; the sentence they were quoting was the row above them.** ➡️ **The rule I'd hand forward: when a filed remedy is described as costing SECONDS and has waited FIRES, the discrepancy IS the finding — go read the authority by coordinate, because a deferral repeated three times has usually been inherited rather than re-decided.**
1019:✅ **F-1376-1 — CURE LANDED s1378 `7a2780be` (its "§7.7 forbids it" premise REFUTED — see F-1378-1); the filed substitution text matched 0 occurrences and was corrected on landing. (s1376, MEASURED — THE LAW'S OWN CENSUS OF ITS MANDATORY BATTERY HAS DRIFTED, AND UNLIKE s1375's ARITHMETIC RESIDUE THIS ONE IS ACTIONABLE IN THE WRONG DIRECTION. `scripts/fire.md` F-1300-4 STATES `test:ledger-guards` IS "THOSE **EIGHT** AND NOTHING ELSE — **36 TESTS**". MEASURED TODAY: **ELEVEN GUARDS / 12 LEAF FILES, 38 TESTS**. THE THREE ADDITIONS WERE ROOTED IN DELIBERATELY, EACH WITH A STATED REASON — SO THE BATTERY IS RIGHT AND THE LAW TEXT IS STALE.)** 🧭 **THE PROBE.** s1375 §K(3) handed forward no hypothesis and prescribed the shape instead: verify the duties, take ONE bounded question the mechanisms cannot answer, STOP. I took the one advisory in the fleet tooling that has **never been measured** — `lane-usable.mjs:241` prints, whenever `package.json` is among a lane's run-surface drift: *"this lane's npm GATES **may be** a strict SUBSET of main's, so a green here can mean less than a green on main. Diff it before trusting a gate."* A hedged quantifier on a load-bearing claim (the runner gates on the lane) that nobody had ever run down. ✅ **RESULT 1 — THE ADVISORY IS VINDICATED, AND THE LANES ARE INNOCENT.** All four lanes' `test:ledger-guards` is a literal **strict prefix** of main's, stopping after `npm run test:citations` and omitting three trailing components: `npm run test:desk-declaration`, `status-archive-audit.mjs --limit 40 --quiet`, `attended-owed-audit.mjs`. The false-green hazard is real as described. **But it is fully attributable to known staleness and NOT to divergence:** all three postdate every lane base (added to main 2026-08-01 **15:19** `73329e15`, **19:05** `128129aa`, **19:48** `bb69ee07`; lane bases are 08-01 **12:13** `46033151` and **14:34** `5fb63bdb`). No lane is broken, no lane holds a divergent gate (**EXTRA lane-only scripts = 0, same-name-different-body = 0 outside these two**), and the standing lane-refresh cure (F-1320-2) already covers it. *I report the innocent verdict as the result rather than dressing staleness up as a finding.* ⚠️ **RESULT 2 — THE ROW: THE LAW'S NUMBER IS A FROZEN SNAPSHOT OF A SET THE LAW ITSELF ENCOURAGES TO GROW.** `scripts/fire.md` line 23 (F-1300-4) closes with *"`test:ledger-guards` is now those **eight** and nothing else — **36 tests**, seconds, not a second battery."* Resolved and re-measured on live main: **12 leaf guard files / 11 distinct guards** (`ruling-propagation` is two files), and the `node --test` arm reports **38 tests / 38 pass / 0 fail**, with all 7 standalone guards rc=0 — **BATTERY GREEN.** The three additions beyond s1301's eight are `desk-declaration-guard` (s1334, F-1334-2), `status-archive-audit` (s1341, F-1341-2) and `attended-owed-audit` (s1343, F-1343-1) — each rooted into this battery **on purpose, with its reason in the commit message**. 🎯 **WHY THIS IS SHARPER THAN A COUNT BEING OFF BY THREE: "AND NOTHING ELSE" IS A CLOSED-SET ASSERTION, NOT ARITHMETIC.** s1375's residue was a sum that did not add up — inert, because nothing acts on a total. This one names a **boundary**, and a diligent reader restoring the law's stated shape would **prune three live guards back to eight**. The clause would then have removed, by its own authority, exactly the guards that F-1300-4's own principle exists to add: *fires mutate ledger rows, law surfaces and gate topology late in their own run, so the battery that catches them must grow as those surfaces grow.* **The law froze a census of a set it commands to expand.** 🔬 **THE METHOD NOTE, AND IT IS A CONFESSION BEFORE IT IS A LESSON: MY FIRST MEASUREMENT WAS WRONG AND WOULD HAVE FILED A FALSE FINDING AGAINST A CORRECT COMMENT.** I first read the gate bodies by regexing them for `.mjs/.js/.ts` paths — which returned **7** files for main and made `test:desk-declaration` look absent from `test:ledger-guards`, so `lane-usable.mjs:113`'s comment naming it read as a category error (an npm script name misfiled among guard files). It is not an error. **Five of the battery's components are `npm run X` indirections, and a path-regex cannot see them.** The true membership had to be resolved **transitively** through `package.json`'s script graph. ➡️ **The reusable half: a gate's membership is not readable from its body when the body COMPOSES other gates — "what does this battery run?" is a graph question wearing a string question's clothes, and the string answer is confidently short.** ⓘ **Second, smaller instrument check, kept because a green you cannot explain is not clean:** my runner first reported `0 tests` on a passing arm — this node build's reporter prints `ℹ tests 38`, not `# tests 38`. Resolved **before** quoting any number, not after. 🪤 **THE CURE, TRAP-CHECKED BEFORE PROPOSING (s1374's rule).** Strict in-line substitution at `scripts/fire.md` line 23: `is now those **eight** and nothing else — **36 tests**` → `is now those **eight** as of s1301, since GROWN DELIBERATELY to **eleven** (s1334 desk-declaration, s1341 status-archive-audit, s1343 attended-owed-audit) — **38 tests**; this set is MEANT to grow as law/ledger/gate surfaces do, so COUNT it, never PRUNE to the number written here`. Characters, no new line. **Trap check run, not inherited:** `grep -rnoE 'fire\.md:[0-9]+'` across all six law surfaces = **0 hits**, so nothing cites `fire.md` by coordinate and this edit rots no guarded pointer. 📋 **FILED, NOT LANDED** — `fire.md` is the fire protocol's own constitution and §7.7 plus the standing order forbid drive-by edits to it, exactly as s1374 and s1375 handled their symmetric fixes. **Latent, not live: the battery is green and correct today; the defect is that the law describes it wrongly in a way a future fire could enforce.** Attended/owner, ~30 seconds. 💡 **THE THROUGH-LINE THIS EXTENDS.** s1374: the mechanism may already have done your job — ask its denominator's edge. s1375: measure what widening would SWEEP IN, not only what it would catch. **s1376: the mechanism GREW past the law that describes it — so when a law states a set's SIZE, check the set, because a census of a living set is a defect with a delay fuse.**
1021:✅ **F-1375-1 — CURE LANDED s1378 `7a2780be` (its "§7.7 forbids it" premise REFUTED — see F-1378-1). (s1375, MEASURED — A NEGATIVE RESULT THAT RETIRES A QUESTION, PLUS ONE LIVE ARITHMETIC DEFECT IN THE CENSUS THAT DEFINES THE LAW CORPUS. s1374 ASKED WHAT `law-pointer-guard` DOES NOT REACH AND ANSWERED FOR ITS *EXTENSION* EDGE; I ASKED THE ADJACENT UNASKED QUESTION — ITS *SURFACE-SET* EDGE — AND THE BOUNDARY TURNS OUT TO BE CORRECT BY MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN BY JUDGEMENT, WHILE THE CLAUSE THAT ENUMERATES THAT CORPUS DOES NOT ADD UP.)** 🧭 **THE PROBE, AND WHY IT IS NOT A RE-RUN.** s1374 §K(2) banked its law-pointer sweep as explicitly do-not-re-derive (23 pointers / 7 surfaces / PASS) and §K(3) handed forward no hypothesis. So I did not re-measure it. `law-pointer-guard.mjs:68` reads **six** surfaces (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `scripts/fire.md`, the three `.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md`). But `scripts/fire.md` §3.0b's own census enumerates the law corpus as *those files **plus every `^- **s9` bullet in `STATUS.md`*** — a seventh surface the guard has never read. If live law is cited there by coordinate, it rots unguarded; that is F-1374-1's hazard class one level up. 📐 **THE MEASUREMENT (re-derived, not inherited — Mistake #4).** `^- **s9` bullets in `STATUS.md` = **140**, matching s1342 exactly. Decomposed: **18 lettered law bullets** (`s9c` `s9d` `s9f` `s9g` `s9h` `s9i` `s9j` `s9k` `s9u` `s9v` `s9ab` `s9af` `s9ag` `s9al` `s9an` `s9ar` `s9at` `s9au`) · **119 numeric handoff archives** · **and 3 bare `- **s9 ` VM-era env bullets** (`env delta`, `provisioning recipe additions`, `env probe` — `STATUS.md` 2363 / 2364 / 2366). ⚠️ **THE DEFECT: 18 + 119 = 137, NOT 140.** §3.0b states the split as *"**140 total = 18 genuine lettered law bullets** — `s9i`/`s9ab`/`s9al`/`s9ar`/… — **plus 119 numeric handoff archives**"*, and that clause exists **precisely** to stop the loose phrase "140 law bullets" over-stating the law corpus 7.8×. It leaves **3 bullets in neither bucket** — and they are the one genuinely ambiguous class: VM-era env bullets that are obsolete for native fires, **one of which self-labels "(BINDING probes for every session)"**. A census written to prevent an over-count carries a 3-bullet residue whose members read as binding. ✅ **WHY THIS IS 🟢 AND NOT 🔺 — I TESTED THE CONCLUSION, NOT ONLY THE COUNT.** s1342's census existed to establish that *"detached worktree"* appears in the corpus **only** at `CLAUDE.md:50` (Mistake #12), the fact on which §3.0b's "written into NO law surface for 47 fires" rests. Re-measured: the 3-bullet residue contains **0** occurrences; corpus-wide the only hits are `CLAUDE.md` ×1 (Mistake #12) and `scripts/fire.md` ×1 (§3.0b's own clause), with `AGENTS.md` **0** and all three `.claude/skills/**/SKILL.md` **0**. **The arithmetic is wrong and the conclusion it supports is intact.** Refuting a count does not refute the claim standing beside it — and saying so plainly is the difference between a correction and a false alarm. 🔍 **THE NEGATIVE RESULT WORTH BANKING, WHICH RETIRES THE QUESTION PERMANENTLY.** All **18** lettered law bullets cite **0** `file:line` coordinates. All **3** bare bullets cite **0**. So widening `SURFACES` to `STATUS.md` would gain the guard **exactly zero live-law pointers** — while sweeping in **1,436** coordinates from `STATUS.md` as a whole (the 119 numeric archives hold only **4**; the remaining ~1,432 live in line-1 and the verbose `- **sNNNN handoff (line-1 archive):**` bullets). 🚫 **THEREFORE: DO NOT WIDEN `SURFACES` TO `STATUS.md`.** It is 1,436 historical claims taken on to guard 0 live ones — and **archived handoff coordinates are *supposed* to rot**, because they record what was true when written; guarding them would red the board on purpose. The guard's boundary is right, and it is now right *for a measured reason* rather than by nobody having asked. 🪤 **THE CURE — AND IT IS TRAP-FREE, WHICH IS THE CONTRAST WORTH KEEPING.** In-line substitution in `scripts/fire.md` §3.0b: `plus 119 numeric handoff archives` → `plus 119 numeric handoff archives and 3 bare "- **s9 " VM-era env bullets (obsolete on native)`. Characters, no new line. **I ran the trap-check s1374 taught before proposing it:** nothing in the corpus cites `fire.md` **or** `STATUS.md` by coordinate (`grep -rnoE 'fire\.md\s*:\s*[0-9]+'` and the `STATUS.md` equivalent across all six surfaces — **0 hits each**), so this edit rots no guarded pointer. F-1374-1's near-identical cure **was** trapped, by `CLAUDE.md:50` sixteen lines below §10b. ➡️ **The reusable half: the same class of cure is trapped on one law surface and free on another, and nothing about the edit tells you which — only the citation check does. Run it before proposing, not after landing.** 📋 **FILED, NOT LANDED**, matching s1374's handling of the symmetric CLAUDE.md fix: `fire.md` is the fire protocol's own constitution and the standing order forbids drive-by edits to it (§7.7). **Latent, not live** — the residue is VM-era and already covered by the protocol's blanket "the VM-era laws are OBSOLETE FOR YOU". Attended/owner, ~20 seconds. ⓘ **The honest footnote:** I opened this expecting to find unguarded coordinates in the law bullets and to recommend widening the guard. The measurement said the opposite, twice over — zero to gain, 1,436 to lose — and the only defect on the road was an arithmetic slip in the sentence that sent me looking. **A probe aimed at a suspected gap is still worth running when it comes back empty, provided you report the empty as the result rather than hunting for a consolation finding.**
1027:🟢 **F-1372-1 (s1372, MEASURED — NEGATIVE RESULT: NO SPEC SLICE IS LOST, BECAUSE SLICE IDS ARE NOT THE LEDGER’S KEY EITHER — AND THE NEW PART IS THAT ABSENCE FROM THE LEDGER IS *BIDIRECTIONAL*, SO THIS ENTIRE CLASS OF SWEEP HAS A SIGN AMBIGUITY AT ITS CORE.)** 🧭 **THE PROBE.** s1370 §K(3) offered two surfaces as *hypotheses, not work*; s1371 took the first (`reviews/` F-ids) and deliberately left the second. This is the second and last: **`specs/**` slices whose playable checkpoints no goal leaf claims.** Per s1371 §K(3) I derived what enumerates the set before counting it, and per s1371 §H(3) **every absence-grep in this fire ran UNCHAINED (`;`, never `&&`)**. 📐 **THE DENOMINATOR HAD TO BE DERIVED, AND THE DOCUMENT-CLASS TRAP s1371 PREDICTED IS REAL.** `specs/` = **77 files / 41 directories** and is **not one class**: RATIFIED specs · DRAFTs · **SEED / “DISCUSSION STATUS, NOT BUILDABLE”** docs (`token-connection`, `loot-and-builds`, `contract-editor`) · a **SUPERSEDED** spec (`outlaw-intelligence`) · **content bundles** (`epoch-saga/e3..e10`) · **recipes** (`town-3d/RECIPE.md`) · **file-per-slice dirs** (`m0`/`m1`/`m2`/`visual-polish`, where the ID is the *filename*). Slice IDs are uppercase tokens declared as `- **RF-01 — …**` or `SLICE PC-01:`. Extracting from declaration-shaped lines only: **133 candidates**, of which I dropped **5 measured false positives** (`F-1`..`F-5` in `e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md` are **finding ids inside a spec** — verified by reading `:265-269`) and **17 BUILD-PLAN per-epoch work-class templates** (`ENG-1`/`CON-1`/`ART-1`/`CER-1` recur for every epoch E2–E10; they are a *plan* vocabulary, not one spec’s slices) ⇒ **111 slice IDs**. ⚖️ **THE STRUCTURAL RESULT, AND IT SETTLES THE PREMISE BEFORE THE RESIDUE MATTERS: 60 in `goals.json` · 95 in `BACKLOG` · 60 in BOTH · 0 in goals-only.** **`goals.json` is a STRICT SUBSET of BACKLOG.** So the question as posed — *“no goal leaf claims it”* — would have reported **51 misses**, and **35 of those are lawfully tracked BACKLOG rungs**. Asking the goal tree is asking the wrong index, exactly as F-ids were the wrong index in F-1371-1. ✅ **THE 16 IN NEITHER, ALL READ AT SOURCE, NOT SAMPLED — ALL 16 LAWFUL, IN FOUR DISTINCT WAYS.** **(1) `ST-00`..`ST-07` (8 — the largest block, and the one that looked like a real finding):** `specs/e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md` is headed **RATIFIED 2026-08-01** by the owner *(“(Q1) option (a) (Q2) option (a) (Q3) option (a)”)*, so 8 slices of an owner-ratified spec appear in no ledger. **Innocent, and already known:** the ruling’s scope clause is ***post-launch*** — recorded at `BACKLOG:2406` and `specs/e10-static-mechanic-DRAFT.md:3` — and **F-1363-1 (s1363) already found the one surface that had lost the qualifier and cured it in `f1308ee9` with an explicit DO-NOT-AUTHOR.** Post-launch is unsatisfied today (`git tag` carries no version tag). **(2) `W1-02`, `W1-06` (2): SHIPPED.** `reviews/w1-02-living-water.md` and `reviews/w1-06-vista.md` exist and `vista` is live in **6 `src/` files**; their ladder rows were retired per §4. **(3) `PB-02` (1): SHIPPED at `5a153e95`** — *“✅ PB-01+02 … EVENT PARITY PROVEN”* (`BACKLOG:1358`). **(4) `MP-05`/`MU-01`/`SS-04`/`ED-06`/`ED-07` (5): owner-gated or not-yet-ratified by construction** — MP-05 is *“owner + son, two devices”*, an acceptance **playtest** (co-op is a PARKED named milestone, `BACKLOG:1408`); MU-01 ends *“→ owner picks”*; SS-04 is a DRAFT rung explicitly sequenced *“With/after the Baron task”*; ED-06/07 sit in a **SEED** spec carrying the owner’s own unanswered question (*“Is it overkill? Should we use something existing?”*), ED-07 marked **OWNER-ONLY v1**. ➡️ **THE STRUCTURAL ANSWER, THIRD ROAD TO THE SAME PLACE: THE LEDGER INDEXES WORK BY THREAD AND RUNG NAME, NOT BY EVERY ID TOKEN A SPEC MINTS.** The e10 Static thread is in BACKLOG **48 times** — as *“e10-static-boss”*, *“roster-wiring-e6-e10”*, *“THE STATIC”* — and **never once as `ST-04`**. A set-difference on slice ID