1061:🟡 **F-1355-1 (s1355, MEASURED AT SOURCE + EXECUTED ON MAIN — THE “RECONCILIATION” F-1351-1 BANKED AS CANDIDATE (8) DISSOLVES: `4/25 (16.0%)` WAS NEVER A FLAKE RATE, AND ITS REAL MEANING IS WORSE THAN THE MISREAD ONE.)** F-1329-1 wrote that its deterministic validator rejection *“sits oddly beside the inventory’s 16% flake rate and is worth reconciling”*, and F-1351-1 banked exactly that as candidate **(8)** — *“reconcile a deterministic validator rejection against the inventory’s recorded 4/25 (16.0%) flake rate”*. ✗ **THERE WAS NEVER A CONTRADICTION TO RECONCILE.** `4/25` is not a frequency; it is a **position**. It lives in `logs/suite-red-inventory.md`’s **“Masking candidates”** table (row 7, `:375`), whose column is **“Failing-line / body-lines ratio”** and whose own header sentence reads *“Ranked by the earliest failing line within the test body. Lower ratios leave more of the test unexercised.”* ✓ **RE-DERIVED AT SOURCE:** `e2e/ed-03-placement-validator.spec.ts` opens its test at `:14`, so its body is `:15–:39` = **25 lines**, and the failing line `:18` is body-line **4** — `4/25` exactly. ✓ **The word “flake” never appears on that row**; it appears in the inventory only in narrative sections about *other* tests (`m4-06-embodiment` at 45%, `run-suspend`). ⚠️ **THE TRAP WAS A DIGIT COINCIDENCE, AND IT IS WHY THIS SURVIVED TWO FIRES: the rejection count is 4 and the failing body-line is also 4.** Two unrelated quantities shared a numeral, and the shared numeral read as corroboration. ✓ **THE DETERMINISTIC HALF IS TRUE AND RE-DERIVED THIS FIRE (26 fires on), not inherited** — probe in a detached worktree per §3.0b, `--workers=1` per §3.1: **42 shipped contracts, 4 rejected** — `e5-deepwater-claim`, `e5-stillwater`, `e5-flotilla` each **5× `field_number` on `tileParams.deepwater.waterTile.regions[1..5].depth`**, and `e10-river` **`spawn_edge_required` on `tileParams.lanes.spawnEdges`**. **210 parses (42×5) produced ZERO verdict flips** — deterministic, measur