MEASUREMENT, NOT A CURE, and not owner-gated:** profile one night-shift run, attribute the delta between construction-time and per-tick cost, and only then choose. Raising the test timeout without doing this would hide the finding rather than fix it. 💡 *The reusable shape: **a correctness fix can bill its cost to a different budget than the one it was reviewed against.** This slice fixed a real lie — an agent briefed about objects that did not exist — and paid for it in the throughput property its own spec names as its reason to exist. Neither the master nor the bar asked about wall time; the runner volunteered it, and it is the most consequential number in the run.* GATE: none. No goal leaf yet. ✅ **ANSWERED s1320 — and BOTH of the two candidate causes named above are REFUTED by measurement. The real cause is `terrainSeed()` re-parsing the URL on every noise hash; see the F-1320-1 row directly below, which supersedes this row's diagnosis (but not its numbers, which reproduced exactly).** ✅ **CURED AND SHIPPED s1321 at `992f40661abb437faba6fc2a7ddb8c5f6706f7db`** (review `reviews/f1319-3-terrain-seed-per-sample-url-parse.md`) — the search-keyed cache, i.e. the SAFE of the two cures F-1320-1 measured. Gated `--workers=1`: tsc clean, build 1.90s, new guard green desktop 4.1s + mobile 4.2s zero console errors, **node-guards 205/205 fail 0 including `gr-sim` byte-for-byte replay so determinism is preserved**, Night Shift fixtures **6,635 ms vs ~19.9 s**, terrain3d-default + never-trap 5/5. ⭐ **The guard has TEETH, proven by MUTATION not argument:** reverting `terrainSeed()` to its pre-cure form reds the new spec **Expected 1 / Received 5600** — 28 `URLSearchParams` constructions per `sampleHeight`, independently corroborating the ~36-per-sample attribution — and the tree was restored byte-exact (sha256 `4ec3c755e2c59feb` both sides). It asserts a MECHANISM (derivation count), not wall time, so it cannot be defused by raising a timeout.
1153:🟡 **F-1320-1 — struck s1344, history only (cured by `992f4066`, 2026-08-01T08:49).** ✓ RE-VERIFIED AT SOURCE, not inherited: `terrainSeed()` (`src/world/Terrain.ts:1619-1624`) now memoises through `terrainSeedCache`, keyed on `window.location.search`, and re-parses **only when that string changes** — the per-call `new URLSearchParams` the finding describes is GONE. Cure commit's own message: *"cache the terrain seed per URL search string — 28 URLSearchParams constructions per sampleHeight become 1"*. ⚠️ **F-1319-3 (line 60) is DELIBERATELY LEFT OPEN: its claim is a measured 8.6× fixture-cost RATIO, and I did not re-run that measurement.** The root cause is cured; the ratio is unverified, and striking a parent finding on a child's evidence is exactly how a real red gets closed by inference. ⓘ **This row is the specimen for F-1344-2** (an open 🟡 whose defect was cured in CODE with no closure row anywhere — `findings-state-guard` compares ledger to ledger and is structurally blind to it; double-state was 0 the whole time). ORIGINAL FINDING, retained verbatim: 🟡 **F-1320-1 (s1320, ROOT CAUSE OF F-1319-3 — THE TERRAIN SEED IS RE-PARSED FROM THE URL ON EVERY NOISE HASH, AND IT IS NOT A HEADLESS PROBLEM).** `terrainSeed()` (`src/world/Terrain.ts:1619-1622`) derives the run seed by constructing **a new `URLSearchParams` from `window.location.search` and re-running `normalizeSeed`** — *on every call*. `terrainHash()` (`:1636`) calls it once per hash, `valueNoise()` (`:1624`) calls `terrainHash` **four times**, and `sample()`/`terrainFeatures()` call `valueNoise` ~9 times: **one terrain sample costs roughly 36 URL parses.** 🔬 **A `--cpu-prof` of one `e1-night-shift` episode (19.85 s, 2,618 samples) attributes ~67% of the run to URL parsing:** `parseParams` **41.4% / 8,218 ms**, `normalizeSeed` 14.1% / 2,790 ms, `URLSearchParams` ctor 9.0% / 1,782 ms, `get search` 2.6% / 516 ms — with `terrainHash` (7.1%) and `terrainSeed` (4.2%) as the callers. ⚠️ **Both of F-1319-3's hypotheses are refuted, and I measured rather than argued.** Construction/`placeFree` cost: `nonTickMs` is **indistinguishable between arms** (801–949 ms with zero fixtures, 482–1,178 ms with seven) — refuted. Structure count: seven *working* lanterns cost **+970 ms**, but flipping **those same seven** to `wrecked` costs a further **+16,730 ms** — so the count is ~6% of the delta and `wrecked` is ~94%. Wrecked fixtures were never the disease; they are the symptom that made it *measurable*, because wrecked instances alone fall through `updateRepairs`' cheap `continue` (`BuildSystem.ts:2117`) into `terrainMaxForFootprint` **every tick**. ⚡ **THE CONSEQUENTIAL HALF: this is not headless-only.** `terrainSeed()` early-outs only on `typeof window === 'undefined'`; **in a browser `window` is always defined**, so the shipped game pays the same ~36-parses-per-sample on every terrain sample — including `Terrain.sample`, which the hero ground-height lookup calls **every frame**. The headless runner did not create this cost, it merely has no frame budget to hide it in. 📐 **Cure measured BOTH ways on the merged tree, both bit-for-bit determinism-preserving (`eventLogHash` stayed `fnv1a32:c086ef19`, `timeMs` `126167`, identical tick count 3,785):** search-keyed cache **19,048 → 3,704 ms (5.1×)**, drop-in and self-invalidating; naive memoise-once **19,048 → 2,174 ms (8.8×)** but requires explicit invalidation at the four `replaceState`/`pushState` seed-rewriting sites (`main.ts:204/219`, `DebugEraSeed.ts:35`, `DeterminismHarness.ts:68`, `TownScene.ts:1143`). **Recommendation: the search-keyed cache** — 5.1× for four lines, and a missed invalidation site in the faster option produces *wrong terrain*, which is far worse than 1.5 s. ⓘ Both s1319 arms' hashes (`84c22e10`, `c086ef19`) reproduced exactly, so its before/after table is independently confirmed; the tree was restored byte-exact after every probe (`git diff -- src/` empty). ➡️ **QUEUED s1320 as `lane-d-f1319-3-terrain-seed-per