public/skill.md:12:Your objective is to secure the posted contract. Read each view before acting; its briefing and mechanics describe the current claim. A run that dies or hits an external cap is not secured and must not be submitted as a standing.
public/skill.md:25:`--contract` is required. `--seed` defaults to `gold-rush`. `--policy` accepts `stdin` (default) or `idle`; idle runs without asking for orders. `--mode escort` is accepted only by a contract that declares that mode. `--overtime` banks the secure and keeps riding until death for AP-15's Homesteader's Crown. Its outcome adds `securedWave`, `overtimeWaves`, and `homestead` (`goldPanned`, `goldSpent`, `peakWorks`, `worksByTier`, and `worksLost`); the first post-secure view carries `now.overtime: true`.
public/skill.md:32:4. After the terminal view, read the outcome as the final stdout line: `secured`, `waves`, `timeMs`, `gold`, `kills`, `calls`, and `eventLogHash`.
public/skill.md:34:Malformed or rejected input is reported on stderr as `gr-sim rejected orders: ...`; correct it and send another array. Stderr also carries the speed diagnostic. Do not parse stderr as game state. Ending stdin while the simulator awaits orders is an error. At the ceiling, the runner ends normally and writes an outcome with `secured: false` and `endReason: "wave-ceiling"`. Boss contracts set that ceiling six waves after the later of the secure wave or boss wave, giving the fight its grace window.
